{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter","id":559989,"title":"New Mortal Remains Chapter!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T17:12:39-07:00","id":559989,"title":"New Mortal Remains Chapter!","content":"The new stretch goal (for $93,000) on the Beast: the Primordial Kickstarter is a pdf expansion for Mortal Remains covering Hunters of the Begotten and their relationship with Heroes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:27:50-07:00","id":560027,"title":"","content":"GEEEEEEEEET IIIIIIIITTTTT!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:33:10-07:00","id":560030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter#post559989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new stretch goal (for $93,000) on the Beast: the Primordial Kickstarter is a pdf expansion for Mortal Remains covering Hunters of the Begotten and their relationship with Heroes!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am so ridiculously excited to develop this. <br /> <br /> Mortal Remains is some of the coolest material I've worked with. I can't wait to do more. I've got Hunter on the brain right now, because I'm doing Edo Jidai Hunter in my other browser tab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:36:47-07:00","id":560033,"title":"","content":"Hunter was the first game in nWoD I ran, and I loved the Mortal Remains books for bringing it back to the other gamelines. In certain ways, I kind of view Hunter as the first crossover game, so bringing the two together is lightning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:00:25-07:00","id":560648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560030#post560030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am so ridiculously excited to develop this. <br /> <br /> Mortal Remains is some of the coolest material I've worked with. I can't wait to do more. I've got Hunter on the brain right now, because I'm doing Edo Jidai Hunter in my other browser tab.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope there is some word count for deconstructing the lore behind Beasts in the way that Spirit Slayers, Witch Finders etc did for Mage, Vampire and Werewolf. Due to the brevity of there being only a chapter per line in Mortal Remains, there was in my personal opinion too much emphasis on how each compact or conspiracy dealt with the monsters and not enough on exploring the legends and confusion. Thus many chapters felt like they were summarizing their game lines rather than looking at them through the fog of limited understanding and fear. (Your mileage may vary) This approach was helpful in that it was a good reference to lines I don't own but for the ones I do I felt I was getting too much detail instead of mystery and horror to be the Hunter POV. Which is not an invalid approach, it just wasn't one that served my needs or interests.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head the Demon chapter really did a great job of keeping to the spirit of the Mage, Werewolf and Vampire books: rather than calling out the Strix and Unchained by name, they were judged by their actions first. The institutional demons also added a really cool idea that I actually cannot directly identify what line it comes from, I think it's a nod to the cosmic horror of the God Machine Chronicle but because of the way it was written I can't be completely certain which reinforces the ignorance and confusion of Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","user":"The Cowardly Scion","date":".  Extra words here and there for clarity. 06-19-2015, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:41:30-07:00","id":560750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cowardly Scion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560648#post560648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The institutional demons also added a really cool idea that I actually cannot directly identify what line it comes from, I think it's a nod to the cosmic horror of the God Machine Chronicle but because of the way it was written I can't be completely certain which reinforces the ignorance and confusion of Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally I think they're either the GM's angels that take a building Cover or a form of Infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:54:27-07:00","id":560779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560750#post560750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I think they're either the GM's angels that take a building Cover or a form of Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div> Totally angels, tied to the local Infrastructure that feeds them Essence. The Demon section of the book seems to be dealing with Infernal demons as the &quot;lesser demons,&quot; Unchained as the &quot;Greater Demons,&quot; and angels as the &quot;Institutional Demons.&quot; Hard to tell the difference between the three, they're all pretty demonic. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T08:55:21-07:00","id":560887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560779#post560779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Totally angels, tied to the local Infrastructure that feeds them Essence. The Demon section of the book seems to be dealing with Infernal demons as the &quot;lesser demons,&quot; Unchained as the &quot;Greater Demons,&quot; and angels as the &quot;Institutional Demons.&quot; Hard to tell the difference between the three, they're all pretty demonic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I'm surprised I never picked up on that. <br /> <br /> Anyhow, definitely excited for a Beast chapter! Hunters that co-op Lairs is such a cool idea. I wonder if they will only be able to target Beasts, or if they will be effective against other supernaturals as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:06:28-07:00","id":560892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cowardly Scion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560648#post560648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really hope there is some word count for deconstructing the lore behind Beasts in the way that Spirit Slayers, Witch Finders etc did for Mage, Vampire and Werewolf. Due to the brevity of there being only a chapter per line in Mortal Remains, there was in my personal opinion too much emphasis on how each compact or conspiracy dealt with the monsters and not enough on exploring the legends and confusion. Thus many chapters felt like they were summarizing their game lines rather than looking at them through the fog of limited understanding and fear. (Your mileage may vary) This approach was helpful in that it was a good reference to lines I don't own but for the ones I do I felt I was getting too much detail instead of mystery and horror to be the Hunter POV. Which is not an invalid approach, it just wasn't one that served my needs or interests.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head the Demon chapter really did a great job of keeping to the spirit of the Mage, Werewolf and Vampire books: rather than calling out the Strix and Unchained by name, they were judged by their actions first. The institutional demons also added a really cool idea that I actually cannot directly identify what line it comes from, I think it's a nod to the cosmic horror of the God Machine Chronicle but because of the way it was written I can't be completely certain which reinforces the ignorance and confusion of Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will try to give it more general focus on Beasts like you've mentioned. I don't really like extended diatribes on how the existing groups relate to these things; I like to keep that short because frankly, it's minor guidance that will probably fall apart at the table, and doesn't deliver much value to the reader besides maybe a story idea or two. I tend to favor player options, so I'll have plenty of Compacts, Conspiracies, and Endowments. I feel like player options are really the best way to 'show don't tell' your setting in a way that brings immediate, obvious playability to the table. <br /> <br /> Since, if this happens, I've got some time, what would people like to see? What angles would you want addressed? Tell me about your pet Compact/Conspiracy, and how you think they'd relate to Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:41:18-07:00","id":560907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560887#post560887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyhow, definitely excited for a Beast chapter! Hunters that co-op Lairs is such a cool idea. I wonder if they will only be able to target Beasts, or if they will be effective against other supernaturals as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, Lairs are kind of like the ultimate in Havens/Sanctums/Hollows/etc. So, I imagine there will be some amount of crossover there, dealing with any wards or the like supernaturals have on their homes. Kind of like the Hunter version of home invasion specialists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:42:38-07:00","id":560909,"title":"","content":"Well, if you are taking requests, I would love to see some non-European/North American/Colonial/Egyptian compacts and/or conspiracies.<br /> <br /> I'll spitball some ideas for locations, take em or leave em as you please: <br /> <br /> -Tajikistan<br /> - Mongolia/Siberia/North China (trying to maintain traditions from the Khanates)<br /> - North Korea<br /> - Tanzania<br /> - Sudan<br /> - Bahrain <br /> <br /> I also think it would cool to have a Conspiracy revolving around Hunters trying to work with the God-Machine (or any other highly controlling supernatural force) to try and take out the Beasts. It kind of plays off the theme of trading your freedoms for protection from fear that for better or for worse is an all too common point of discussion in today's society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T09:57:08-07:00","id":560915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=560892#post560892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since, if this happens, I've got some time, what would people like to see? What angles would you want addressed? Tell me about your pet Compact/Conspiracy, and how you think they'd relate to Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's four things that I think really needs to be addressed with Beast hunters.<br /> <br /> 1) Heroes, and how they relate to Hunters. Especially when some hunters see them as allies, and how some see them as threats worse than the Beasts themselves. Or if they can see a difference at all. Unlike most supernaturals, Heroes are the only &quot;bane&quot; that Beasts have. Vamps, Prommies, and Mummies fear fire, wolves and 'lings special metals, mages likely still have True Name issues, etc. So, from a hunter perspective, the hero/beast interaction is critical to their Vigil. Alternatively, making Heroes (the power to steal hero-powers) into a Hunter Conspiracy could be very interesting.<br /> <br /> 2) Lair invasions. This is the big one, I think. Beasts specialize in merging the physical and the monstrous (or, more likely from the hunter's standpoint, making Nightmares real), be it as their body, or as their environment. More than anything, this is what obviously separates the <br /> <br /> 3) Which hunters see the Soul/Horror when an atavism is used, and which don't? Who qualifies as Kin? *cough*Lucifuge*cough*<br /> <br /> 4) Beasts as Evil Overlords. What I mean by this is the tendacy for Beasts to surround themselves with other supernaturals, and how that's going to affect their Vigil. Going against a Beast means you'll need to prepare silver, iron, fire, and salt for other battles long before you fight the Beast itself. And how you can't assume that the people a Beast hangs around with are all other Beasts - a reasonable assumption with anyone else. Likewise, the reverse is true - how to tell when a Beast is hanging out when you're tracking down a witch coven or vampiric brood.<br /> <br /> I don't think that causing Nightmares is going to be a big issue with hunters - yes, it might put you on the trail of a Beast, but I don't think most are going to really worry about something that's only when you sleep. At best, I see a foot note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:31:27-07:00","id":560957,"title":"","content":"Cheiron Group<br /> - Having a very special relationship with Heroes (ala Cheiron of myth)<br /> - Thaumatechnology derived from Atavism/Horror-form that shouldn't necessarily be possible, but their pet Heroes somehow facilitate.<br /> - Psychopharmacological Thaumatech to access to the Primordial Dream - perhaps temporarily giving their Hunters access to Hero Gifts or the ability to tag Anathema.<br /> <br /> What is the Lady of Milan's relationship to the Dark Mother?<br /> <br /> Discussion of a Victorian/Georgian Era Compact of Alienists who sought to &quot;treat&quot; Beasts and Heroes alike. Jung ended up having a close relationship with them. Some precedence for the Talbot Group branching out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T11:45:17-07:00","id":560983,"title":"","content":"Question. Are you planning to do a Conspiracy who play the Moiraine Damodred to the Heroes' Rand al-Thor? Because if you are I'll save myself the effort <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:25:15-07:00","id":561044,"title":"","content":"I've never read Wheel of Time, but they mentioned in the Stretch Goal blurb that the Conspiracy will be coopting Lairs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:40:22-07:00","id":561055,"title":"","content":"If that's the only Conspiracy than it's a no. Is it the only Conspiracy?<br /> <br /> (Think a more manipulative Obi-Wan Kenobi or Gandalf)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:01:17-07:00","id":561067,"title":"","content":"I would like to see the Cheiron Group lives up its name, having some kind of connection between them and Beasts. Their logo is meant to have some meaning, after all.<br /> <br /> describing which Conspiracy members are Kin is a must- it would clear a lot of confusion IMO. Also, detailing some abstract rules for the &quot;spirit quest&quot; which hunters may take to become &quot;adopted&quot; by the Beast could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Hunters vs Heroes- I must say that this angle is as interesting as the Hunter vs Beast angle, if not more. Basic reactions the big groups has toward those guys sounds interesting, even if not necessary. Having at least one group who targets Heroes (even if they simply try to &quot;guide&quot; them, as Kingsraven suggested) looks like something which is really needed. The clearer is the distinction between the two the better. Maybe even exploring the Slasher-Hero connection a bit.<br /> <br /> I personally hope that at least one of the groups would be tied into Australia- both because I think the myths about the Dreamtime in the continent and the way it is sometimes conceptualized as a &quot;land of monsters&quot; from the outside could work thematically for Beast and because Oceania doesn't have hunters at all.<br /> <br /> finally, Beasts not necessary as bad guys. Sure, this is hunter and they are monsters, but Beast is all about making connections. Mentioning that some groups of hunters are gathered to protect Beasts for all kinds of reasons (maybe the Null Mysteriis see them as an &quot;extinct breed&quot; and wants to protect them?) could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:19:51-07:00","id":561075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561067#post561067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">describing which Conspiracy members are Kin is a must- it would clear a lot of confusion IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Under the current draft of Beast (which admittedly is in flux), the Lucifuge are literally the only canon group who qualify. No one else gets their Endowments through bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:20:56-07:00","id":561076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561055#post561055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the only Conspiracy than it's a no. Is it the only Conspiracy?<br /> <br /> (Think a more manipulative Obi-Wan Kenobi or Gandalf)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds more like a cool character concept than a Conspiracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:28:39-07:00","id":561086,"title":"","content":"That's why they work solo <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:39:07-07:00","id":561124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561075#post561075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the current draft of Beast (which admittedly is in flux), the Lucifuge are literally the only canon group who qualify. No one else gets their Endowments through bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beast is a game about choosing your family, not which one you're born to. That's why you develop Kinship from hanging out with them over prolonged periods of time. Choice is the important thing here. So, if you want to get down to it, the Malleus Malificorum could count as easily as Lucifuge; they're mortals with magic. Cherion could do a whole Stockholm Kinship with captive Beasts and their scientist-keepers. Psychic mortals are specifically called out, and that describes the VASCU to a T. The rest are debatable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:49:48-07:00","id":561133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561124#post561124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Beast is a game about choosing your family, not which one you're born to. That's why you develop Kinship from hanging out with them over prolonged periods of time. Choice is the important thing here. So, if you want to get down to it, the Malleus Malificorum could count as easily as Lucifuge; they're mortals with magic. Cherion could do a whole Stockholm Kinship with captive Beasts and their scientist-keepers. Psychic mortals are specifically called out, and that describes the VASCU to a T. The rest are debatable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a perfectly reasonable argument about what thematically should be the case. I however was responding to the explicit statement of the rules that says that only Hunters who inherit their Endowment by Blood are Kin, and explicitly calls out VASCU as not Kin (which isn't actually surprising when you consider that the God-Machine is the likely source of their powers judging by hints in their write-up and we know the Beasts have no kinship there).<br /> <br /> The rules were explicit in the text is all I was saying. Arguments that they should be different is another conversation entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:09:10-07:00","id":561197,"title":"","content":"I would just like to mention that if I'm not mistaken, canonically, VASCU is explicitly said to not be psychics, and that the Wintergreen Process does not awaken psychic abilities- it is just that the powers VASCU has are so similar to psychic powers, that almost everyone would confuse them as psychic powers (which is why psychic merits should be translated into their Endowment after joining VASCU, for they are &quot;nullified&quot;).<br /> <br /> In short, they are psychics who are not psychics. If THAT doesn't reek of the God Machine, I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T17:34:49-07:00","id":561403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561197#post561197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would just like to mention that if I'm not mistaken, canonically, VASCU is explicitly said to not be psychics, and that the Wintergreen Process does not awaken psychic abilities- it is just that the powers VASCU has are so similar to psychic powers, that almost everyone would confuse them as psychic powers (which is why psychic merits should be translated into their Endowment after joining VASCU, for they are &quot;nullified&quot;).<br /> <br /> In short, they are psychics who are not psychics. If THAT doesn't reek of the God Machine, I don't know what is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like the exact opposite of what's been said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T04:53:38-07:00","id":561791,"title":"","content":"Agreeing with all the <b>LostLight </b>post but espeically those points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561067#post561067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters vs Heroes- I must say that this angle is as interesting as the Hunter vs Beast angle, if not more. Basic reactions the big groups has toward those guys sounds interesting, even if not necessary. Having at least one group who targets Heroes (even if they simply try to &quot;guide&quot; them, as Kingsraven suggested) looks like something which is really needed. The clearer is the distinction between the two the better. Maybe even exploring the Slasher-Hero connection a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would add great would be highlighting when one of Hunters become the Hero - cell is working on new monster case, unsaspecting it's a Beast. By few encounters with it's Nightmares, one of cell mates start too act... wierd. Egomanic. Narssistic. He slowly becomes Ahab to the cell's Moby Dick. And what now his cell mates do with him, on trail of Beast?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561067#post561067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally hope that at least one of the groups would be tied into Australia- both because I think the myths about the Dreamtime in the continent and the way it is sometimes conceptualized as a &quot;land of monsters&quot; from the outside could work thematically for Beast and because Oceania doesn't have hunters at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much this! Australia was no exposed in nWoD, and with the relation <b>Beast</b> have with Astral Space - that is very important to natives mythlogies - it would really be missed oportunity if not showing in <b>Mortal Remains</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=561067#post561067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">finally, Beasts not necessary as bad guys. Sure, this is hunter and they are monsters, but Beast is all about making connections. Mentioning that some groups of hunters are gathered to protect Beasts for all kinds of reasons (maybe the Null Mysteriis see them as an &quot;extinct breed&quot; and wants to protect them?) could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Null Mysteriis fixiating on Begotten as lab specimens and going aginst other hunters plan to slay them is very fair point.<br /> <br /> Also, Cheiron Group and thier connection to Beast - maybe Cheiron is collecting Thaumatechnology in the way to replicate Atavisms and Kinship Begotten have with other supernaturls? Basiclly Cheiron wants to be part of Family, on their own, wicked way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-21-2015, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T16:44:34-07:00","id":563524,"title":"","content":"I would like to see ties to mythology and religion, both real world and fictitious, that reflect an awareness of Beasts corrupted by long years of the telephone game and how each Beast is almost a unique creature. Perhaps an emphasis that it is rare to understand that Beasts are all part of a singular family or perhaps they are very often confused for other types of supernatural creature. Perhaps few Hunters know of such a thing as a &quot;Beast&quot; or the &quot;Begotten&quot; and instead assume that Vampires don't really burn in the sun or literally drink blood, these were just metaphors that were mistranslated. They actually feed on fear. Werewolves also exist but they don't actually turn into wolves, just adopt bestial characteristics like enhanced strength and senses while appearing fully human. Nessie? If you see someone suspicious swimming in the lake and stare long enough, sometimes you see a reflection of something that looks a lot like a dinosaur....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T22:50:23-07:00","id":565043,"title":"","content":"I just noticed.<br /> <br /> We got the chapter! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T14:26:05-07:00","id":565756,"title":"","content":"Excited to see how hunters can take over a Lair. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T15:42:05-07:00","id":565809,"title":"","content":"What I'm curious about is what advantage would a hunter get for co-opting a lair? Lairs for beasts are mostly for manifesting one's inner horror or unleashing the environmental tilts.<br /> <br /> Can they somehow enhance themselves within a lair, or do they throw earthquakes, fire, and water at people?<br /> <br /> And if it's latter, are they immune to the environmental tilts, can they make others immune like beasts can? Otherwise, friendly fire might involve literal fire around these guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-23-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T15:57:58-07:00","id":565818,"title":"","content":"Secret hideout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T17:54:50-07:00","id":565899,"title":"","content":"I'm excited <i>because</i> I have no idea what advantage hunters would get from a lair except some weird place to hang out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_lin