stmedia.vresp.com/97ba6aedee/man_stopped_desert.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T03:09:07-07:00","id":880838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=880655#post880655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entered first draft!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. We're writing it right now. It's still super preliminary, but I'm having a lot of fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:06:41-07:00","id":885679,"title":"","content":"Any chance we can get a nibble at what ideas we might see from new groups?<br /> <br /> At the risk of sounding disgustingly weaboo, the new Persona seems to be about folks who can break into the collective unconscious and steal cruelty and oppression out of the minds who cause them. That's one hell of an idea for a Conspiracy if I've ever geard one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:53:03-07:00","id":886804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=568258#post568258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you know, passing on an old list of hunter group ideas I once had, I think that the my pirates of the Caribbean/world explorer conspiracy could work really well as Beast Hunters...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. The Navio de Tolos were one of your best groups, by far.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:31:48-07:00","id":887791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=885679#post885679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance we can get a nibble at what ideas we might see from new groups?<br /> <br /> At the risk of sounding disgustingly weaboo, the new Persona seems to be about folks who can break into the collective unconscious and steal cruelty and oppression out of the minds who cause them. That's one hell of an idea for a Conspiracy if I've ever geard one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. This is SUPER loose, but these are the notes from my original outline. The groups are sort of evolving a bit as I write them.<br /> <br /> Compact 1: The Cult<br /> These guys see Beasts as gods, and gods worthy of only the best tribute. So, they feed Beasts monsters, the way your pet cat leaves you dead birds. It\u2019s certainly well-intentioned, but kinda gross and not very helpful at all. What\u2019s a Beast to do when they wake up surrounded by staked vampires? Well, the Beast tries to stop the people from doing it again. They perceive that as a great epic blessing, they slay the dragon, and they move on to the next biggest dragon since CLEARLY they\u2019re the chosen ones.<br /> <br /> Compact 2: The Minutemen<br /> This is a well-regulated militia full of very armed, very dangerous people with a single guiding philosophy: Monsters exist, but monsters exist because of terrorist Heroes. So, stop the Heroes, and you stop most of the collateral damage from ever happening. Look at these guys like the wet dreams of every Tom Clancy \u201crealpolitik\u201d guy out there. They\u2019re \u201cdoing thankless work\u201d like you might expect in a show like 24.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy: The Dream Warriors<br /> This group takes its inspiration from Nightmare on Elm Street 3. The fact that we\u2019ve never been able to say this in a Chronicles of Darkness book is a crime that I want to correct. Basically, they\u2019re troubled teens trained to be lucid dreamers. In the dreamscapes, they have super powers that look a little like Changeling Oneiromancy (I will make some subtle references that they\u2019re related). Basically, they\u2019re armed in their choice environment, and take the fight to the Beasts in their own realms. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:34:42-07:00","id":887793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887791#post887791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. This is SUPER loose, but these are the notes from my original outline. The groups are sort of evolving a bit as I write them.<br /> <br /> Compact 1: The Cult<br /> These guys see Beasts as gods, and gods worthy of only the best tribute. So, they feed Beasts monsters, the way your pet cat leaves you dead birds. It\u2019s certainly well-intentioned, but kinda gross and not very helpful at all. What\u2019s a Beast to do when they wake up surrounded by staked vampires? Well, the Beast tries to stop the people from doing it again. They perceive that as a great epic blessing, they slay the dragon, and they move on to the next biggest dragon since CLEARLY they\u2019re the chosen ones.<br /> <br /> Compact 2: The Minutemen<br /> This is a well-regulated militia full of very armed, very dangerous people with a single guiding philosophy: Monsters exist, but monsters exist because of terrorist Heroes. So, stop the Heroes, and you stop most of the collateral damage from ever happening. Look at these guys like the wet dreams of every Tom Clancy \u201crealpolitik\u201d guy out there. They\u2019re \u201cdoing thankless work\u201d like you might expect in a show like 24.<br /> <br /> Conspiracy: The Dream Warriors<br /> This group takes its inspiration from Nightmare on Elm Street 3. The fact that we\u2019ve never been able to say this in a Chronicles of Darkness book is a crime that I want to correct. Basically, they\u2019re troubled teens trained to be lucid dreamers. In the dreamscapes, they have super powers that look a little like Changeling Oneiromancy (I will make some subtle references that they\u2019re related). Basically, they\u2019re armed in their choice environment, and take the fight to the Beasts in their own realms. </div> </div> </div> </div>Mister Hill, you may well be finally selling me on Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:41:19-07:00","id":887800,"title":"","content":"I actually used the title name &quot;Minutemen&quot; at my table for the right-wing splinter of the Union that didn't want to be associated with organized labor. Easily could work as the same guys (though I think for my purposes it'll be more TF: VALKYRIE going &quot;24&quot; on domestic terrorist-'Heroes')","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:44:02-07:00","id":887804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887793#post887793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mister Hill, you may well be finally selling me on Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm going to say this in hopes that people read it generously. I understand how it could be taken as a negative, but please try not to. I wrote on Beast. <br /> <br /> Writing this has actually sold me on Beast. I feel that it takes the same core material, and expresses it in slightly different light because of the Hunter bias. And since Hunters are neither Beasts nor Heroes, you get some unique perspective that I feel may have actually helped the Beast core book in retrospect. Thinking about it all in this terms has made me want to play in a game, and really sink my teeth into the material more. I hope it does the same for others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:45:06-07:00","id":887806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887800#post887800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually used the title name &quot;Minutemen&quot; at my table for the right-wing splinter of the Union that didn't want to be associated with organized labor. Easily could work as the same guys (though I think for my purposes it'll be more TF: VALKYRIE going &quot;24&quot; on domestic terrorist-'Heroes')</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually considering making them a TF:V splinter group. The idea would be that mainstream TF:V interprets Heroes as humans, and so not their jurisdiction. These guys were like, &quot;Fuck that.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:12:05-07:00","id":887835,"title":"","content":"I lean against that because I find the idea that VALKYRIE considers many other Hunters (to say nothing of Heroes) to be dangerous vigilantes and terrorists that do fall under their purview to try and keep in-line, quiet, etc - to open more plot doors than it closes.<br /> <br /> Of course my take on VALKYRIE is that they knowingly accept the existence of many powerful supernatural conspiracies and if anything use their work to prop those dominant groups up in the name of stability, like the U.S. Government and certain Middle Eastern (and historically Latin American) dictatorships. And thus are prone to come down hard on Hunters who do things like go after certain entrenched supernatural powers that enforce the Masquerade and the like.<br /> <br /> That's what I swapped out their leadership working FOR vampires for. It's not that they're puppets. It's that they make hard compromises like that all the time, and accept, and even protect, a certain amount of supernatural nefariousness to stop all out wars in America's streets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-11-2016, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:34:23-07:00","id":887859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887804#post887804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I'm going to say this in hopes that people read it generously. I understand how it could be taken as a negative, but please try not to. I wrote on Beast.<br /> <br /> Writing this has actually sold me on Beast. I feel that it takes the same core material, and expresses it in slightly different light because of the Hunter bias. And since Hunters are neither Beasts nor Heroes, you get some unique perspective that I feel may have actually helped the Beast core book in retrospect. Thinking about it all in this terms has made me want to play in a game, and really sink my teeth into the material more. I hope it does the same for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the ideal reaction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T22:35:26-07:00","id":887902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887804#post887804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm going to say this in hopes that people read it generously. I understand how it could be taken as a negative, but please try not to. I wrote on Beast. <br /> <br /> Writing this has actually sold me on Beast. I feel that it takes the same core material, and expresses it in slightly different light because of the Hunter bias. And since Hunters are neither Beasts nor Heroes, you get some unique perspective that I feel may have actually helped the Beast core book in retrospect. Thinking about it all in this terms has made me want to play in a game, and really sink my teeth into the material more. I hope it does the same for others.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see. Beast was the first Onyx Path gameline that I took a pass on; and I say that with disappointment because I <i>wanted</i> to like it. With that in mind, I'm hoping that this Mortal Remains extension does for Beast what Beast did not do for itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T00:00:11-07:00","id":887949,"title":"","content":"It sounds like I'm in a slightly different boat to most people. I agreed with the criticisms of draft one, the really harsh ones. I thought draft two made for some brilliant antagonists in that I felt the idea of teaching lessons through fear (especially with the conflict of interest called Hunger) was so spectacularly immoral (by human standards Arc <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) that you could create great Hunter based around a rebuttal. But I just couldn't see how you'd create any story longer than a session out of it. I couldn't see why a storyteller planning a werewolf game would thing &quot;what this pack needs is a Beast&quot; or why I'd prefer to use Beast over Mage or Hunter for an investigating diverse mysteries game.<br /> <br /> So sadly, I don't think this game could sell me on Beast. The book that has a shot is the Beast Storyteller's guide.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll need to see more of the groups before I can really comment. I was hoping that at least one of the groups would be able to address the philosophical themes of Beast and prevent counter arguements. A group who can give a convincing reason why teaching through fear is a bad idea. Or a group who helps monsters and can give a convincing reason why Beasts are enablers and a harmful influence on their kin. From your descriptions it doesn't look like we're getting that, but maybe the full write up will surprise me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887806#post887806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually considering making them a TF:V splinter group. The idea would be that mainstream TF:V interprets Heroes as humans, and so not their jurisdiction. These guys were like, &quot;Fuck that.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887835#post887835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course my take on VALKYRIE is that they knowingly accept the existence of many powerful supernatural conspiracies and if anything use their work to prop those dominant groups up in the name of stability, like the U.S. Government and certain Middle Eastern (and historically Latin American) dictatorships. And thus are prone to come down hard on Hunters who do things like go after certain entrenched supernatural powers that enforce the Masquerade and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do something similar with a TF:V - Vampire relationship. However I limit this dark alliance just to Vampires. (In fact, my justification is that they had a McCarthy panic attack when they started to notice Free Councilers in counter-culture groups and teamed up with vampires to prevent any possible witch led Soviet invasion)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T00:02:36-07:00","id":887953,"title":"","content":"I must say that the thing look forward the most in the chapter is the Cheiron Group's write up. Yeah, the new groups sounds pretty cool- but not I'll be really disappointed if all their writeup would say is &quot;they kill Beasts and put their organs into them, and has some basic understanding of the creature&quot;. Especially after that frighting fiction in Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T00:03:42-07:00","id":887954,"title":"","content":"I specifically left it open to be adaptable, but yeah it's primarily Invictus. They have some Panopticon infiltration at my table, but no one is aware of it yet (they're not calling the shots, but they've gotten their foot in the door).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T01:34:47-07:00","id":887984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887953#post887953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that the thing look forward the most in the chapter is the Cheiron Group's write up. Yeah, the new groups sounds pretty cool- but not I'll be really disappointed if all their writeup would say is &quot;they kill Beasts and put their organs into them, and has some basic understanding of the creature&quot;. Especially after that frighting fiction in Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some real potential for Cheiron here.<br /> <br /> Namtaru can be Nightmares of Disease. So Cheiron going &quot;the black plauge? You're not scary, you're not even relevent anymore&quot; could be pretty cool. Alternatively cutting some under the table deals to spread fear of diseases - ranging from &quot;no one is buying our expensive medicine because bed rest is better value for money&quot; to &quot;people are dying because of anti-vax nonsense, make them scared of mumps instead&quot;. With a few implants Cheiron could qualify as Kin after all.<br /> <br /> Or for opposing Beasts. &quot;My contract say if I meet quota I get to put company resources on a personal issue. People are so scared of their children being autistic (Anakim rather than Namtaru I think) that they're avoiding life saving vaccines. So I'm taking some heavily armed company resources to kill the fear of your child being autistic&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> This might also be an opportunity to add another possible origin* for Cheiron. Centaurs were monsters, but mythological Cheiron was basically the one good Centaur. Perhaps Cheiron was a Beast who turned his back on monstrousness by never spending Satity and thus never needing to feed. Or perhaps he turned doctors into kin using Thaumatechnology, taught them medicine so that they could &quot;hunt&quot; sickness and provide 100% ethical Family Dinners.<br /> <br /> This could mean that Cheiron knows the mythic side of Beasts, and have Thaumatechnology to get into Lairs, after all a Horror will have more interesting body parts than a human. In fact, the whole thing about Hercules using the Neman Lion's pelt as armour or Perseus using Medusa's head as a weapon could be the core foundation of Thaumatechnology. A bit of chopped Horror to impose mythic rather than scientific/occult laws. Hunted rather than farmed monsters so the powers are earned, and suddenly impossible transplants might not even have side effects.<br /> <br /> * I like the idea that Cheiron has fallen apart several times in history and each time it has been rebuilt by someone discovering the remains of the previous Cheiron. But one of those groups has to be the origonal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:59:42-07:00","id":888067,"title":"","content":"A well informed Cheiron operative could be a Beast's worst nightmare. If we assume a Beast's Horror is beyond Cheiron's reach, there is little of interest to be harvested. Beasts are physically human after all. However, if one creates an in-depth psychological profile they can then torment the Beast by targeting their connections and exploiting their weaknesses until the targets snaps. Then, when their body shifts and transforms, <i>then</i> you send in the harvesting crew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:53:15-07:00","id":888196,"title":"","content":"In my own mist shrouded mythology of Hunter the first Cheiron Group was the cell of disciples that gravitated towards an experienced hunter in the ancient near east. He was one of the first to be a true terror to the monsters beyond the fire, being a precocious horseman and an expert in rites of extispicy. He trained many new hunters over his long years, and one of these disciples would spell the doom of their cell. The disciple was a troubled man plagued by manias but he was a tremendous warrior in their battles against the unnatural, and their leader thought he could be focused with training. The problem was that the disciple wasn't just a hunter, he was a Hero. He would never be able to rest until he finished his bloody labors, and anyone who stood in his way even for a moment would become a footnote in his great destiny. He betrayed and murdered their master, breaking the cell and scattering it for centuries until it passed into legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:58:15-07:00","id":888201,"title":"","content":"This also reminds me I need to finish my own dream-focused Compact and get it up here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:40:55-07:00","id":888242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887791#post887791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compact 1: The Cult<br /> These guys see Beasts as gods, and gods worthy of only the best tribute. So, they feed Beasts monsters, the way your pet cat leaves you dead birds. It\u2019s certainly well-intentioned, but kinda gross and not very helpful at all. What\u2019s a Beast to do when they wake up surrounded by staked vampires? Well, the Beast tries to stop the people from doing it again. They perceive that as a great epic blessing, they slay the dragon, and they move on to the next biggest dragon since CLEARLY they\u2019re the chosen ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm somewhat worried about this one. As it stands, it appears to be solely an antagonist Compact, since it already limits the way Hunter-Beast interaction progresses. There are so many ways such a relationship could mess with both sides. With different expectations from the Cult, different means of appeasement and different Beasts possibilities would only grow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:09:49-07:00","id":888270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888242#post888242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm somewhat worried about this one. As it stands, it appears to be solely an antagonist Compact, since it already limits the way Hunter-Beast interaction progresses. There are so many ways such a relationship could mess with both sides. With different expectations from the Cult, different means of appeasement and different Beasts possibilities would only grow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it sounds pretty fine as is, but what I'm curious about is <i>why</i> they do it. Why do they worship Beasts? Why is being noticed by them such a blessing? What do they get out of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:44:11-07:00","id":888298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888270#post888270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it sounds pretty fine as is, but what I'm curious about is <i>why</i> they do it. Why do they worship Beasts? Why is being noticed by them such a blessing? What do they get out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>They get to sleep soundly, knowing the dragon won't pick one of their daughters tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:56:55-07:00","id":888308,"title":"","content":"the nice thing is that the Beasts doesn't enjoy that extra attention- they are stuck around a bunch of fanboys who just decide to &quot;please&quot; their dragon the way they think it wants to be pleased. From how I read their preview, the &quot;blessing&quot; in the situation is the fact they participate in the Epic of &quot;slaying the beast&quot;- maybe they even believe that the fact the &quot;god&quot; decides it had enough of their shit and attack them is the way it answers their &quot;tributes&quot;- for from their point of view, it means the Beast has decided to allow itself getting killed by its worshipers. That means that if the first monsters they kill don't make their god descend on them, they need better sacrifices- something that the Beast truly desires. Like that vampire she hangs with a lot lately, or that pack of shifters she regularly hunts with. It is obvious that the Beast likes those monsters- and so by sacrificing them to it, they would please their god enough to bless them with its presence in person, giving them the right to kill it with their own hands.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm pretty sure Heroes would be pissed off from the Minutemen- beasts are the ones who rise heroes, fears gives power to courage. Such misunderstanding would surely make the common Hero very pissed off (and perhaps even the common beast, but they won't be stupid enough to correct the hunters, I think). Of course, that is if they'll even bother speaking with them. Heroes expect hunters to be follow, and don't seem to be interested in what they have to say. It also makes me wonder how would an imprisoned Hero in the hands of VASCU or a similar group with access to psychologists would feel when he tries to explain his &quot;therapist&quot; his roll in the monomyth, why what he does is so important and all the other dream symbolism of their Journey.<br /> <br /> As for the Dream Warriors- I assume those are the guys who co-opt Lairs? I assume that the idea of astral-projecting hunters who fight the nightmares of mankind was bound to happen. Not that I say they are not cool- they sound like a great concept and I wait for more about them, but I still hoped for an Australian group who search the Dreamtime for beasts, or maybe some corporation who takes over Lairs and terraform them for its own needs. Oh well.<br /> <br /> EDIT- Arc's interpretation is also a lot more simple and likely, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:25:46-07:00","id":888335,"title":"","content":"Arc's interpretation makes sense for sane Hunters. Yours makes sense for the Cult as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:28:54-07:00","id":888342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888335#post888335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc's interpretation makes sense for sane Hunters. Yours makes sense for the Cult as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a fallacy here.<br /> <br /> I rarely assume Hunters are sane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:33:20-07:00","id":888347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888308#post888308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or maybe some corporation who takes over Lairs and terraform them for its own needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, a criminal smuggling enterprise could get a lot of mileage out of Primordial Pathways...<br /> <br /> And despite being memetic fear-based dream monsters, Horrors aren't immune to damage or Tilts and Conditions (unless they are Traits of its Lair). I don't think Drugged is one of those...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-11-2016, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T10:35:23-07:00","id":888350,"title":"","content":"Oh, touch\u00e9!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:35:30-07:00","id":888406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888298#post888298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They get to sleep soundly, knowing the dragon won't pick one of their daughters tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Appeasement and deflection are reasons I can get behind. The question is I suppose, does it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T11:47:07-07:00","id":888418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888406#post888406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appeasement and deflection are reasons I can get behind. The question is I suppose, does it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely depends on the Beast. Does it need to? If it doesn't, maybe it means the sacrifices just weren't <i>enough</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:23:43-07:00","id":888502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888347#post888347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, a criminal smuggling enterprise could get a lot of mileage out of Primordial Pathways...</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Ascending Ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> IMO they use the Underworld for these kinds of shnanigans. The Upper Reaches are probably the safest otherworld, except for the possibility of getting lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888308#post888308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Dream Warriors- I assume those are the guys who co-opt Lairs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wondered about that too. I am quite besotted with the idea of a &quot;taming the wild&quot; themed Conspiracy, with the signature charachter bing based on Yacouba Sawadogo.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:37:31-07:00","id":888522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888502#post888502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean the Ascending Ones <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> IMO they use the Underworld for these kinds of shnanigans. The Upper Reaches are probably the safest otherworld, except for the possibility of getting lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>But think of what this represents: Conquering Fears-made-manifest, keeping it subdued through enlightened alchemy, and laying claim to a portion of the collective human soul... to transport your narcotics without interference by customs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:56:49-07:00","id":888533,"title":"","content":"Admittedly that's hilarious. But you could spin something similar for the Underworld <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:59:56-07:00","id":888587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888406#post888406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appeasement and deflection are reasons I can get behind. The question is I suppose, does it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>It works better on golds than reds, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:18:57-07:00","id":888759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888522#post888522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But think of what this represents: Conquering Fears-made-manifest, keeping it subdued through enlightened alchemy, and laying claim to a portion of the collective human soul... to transport your narcotics without interference by customs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had something like this feature in a game a while back. There was a hollow under a tree that led to other places. The folks who first discovered it dug it out into a cellar and put it to the most logical use at hand: smuggling moonshine during Prohibition. Eventually the feds caught up with them and not really knowing what to do with the weird secret room that was nowhere the land ended up in the hands of Task Force Valkyrie. Operation Fort had some fun with it for a couple decades before their funding for scientifically important but organizationally unactionable research dried up in the 80's. Strapped for cash, they decided to start doing what half the other covert groups were doing and began financing their research by using the room to smuggle cocaine. This ended badly. One of their shipments failed to materialize (literally) along with its handlers and the resulting recriminations ended up exposing them. They never figured out what happened to it. Most people assumed somebody got greedy and rerouted it, but a few think it may have accidently gone somewhere... <i>else</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:22:03-07:00","id":888822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887953#post887953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that the thing look forward the most in the chapter is the Cheiron Group's write up. Yeah, the new groups sounds pretty cool- but not I'll be really disappointed if all their writeup would say is &quot;they kill Beasts and put their organs into them, and has some basic understanding of the creature&quot;. Especially after that frighting fiction in Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">While most hunters would unapologetically refer to themselves as &quot;human&quot;, beasts don't care about those classifications. To beasts, some hunters are kin, and there's nothing worse than being betrayed by one's own family. This isn't an issue for most hunters, but those in certain Conspiracies -- namely the Lucifuge -- have inherently complicated relationships with beasts. Other groups have particularly constrained relations with beasts because of the natures of their Vigils. For example, when beasts learn of the Cheiron Group and their morbid Thanatechnology, their typical response is to turn the hunt back on the hunters, to slaughter them, and to slaughter their entire cells. In one egregious example in Tokyo, the Cheiron Group was entirely eradicated by a small group of beasts in order to &quot;reclaim&quot; the bodies of their kin. The Ashwood Abbey has similarly disastrous conflicts with beasts when beasts learn of their methodology. Even the most jaded beast can at least understand why hunters take up the Vigil. This sympathy affords at least reasonable approaches to most hunters. But those hunters who go above and beyond, those who hunt for pleasure or profit, they're given no quarter.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:23:26-07:00","id":888823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887949#post887949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll need to see more of the groups before I can really comment. I was hoping that at least one of the groups would be able to address the philosophical themes of Beast and prevent counter arguements. A group who can give a convincing reason why teaching through fear is a bad idea. Or a group who helps monsters and can give a convincing reason why Beasts are enablers and a harmful influence on their kin. From your descriptions it doesn't look like we're getting that, but maybe the full write up will surprise me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea. Let me see if I can't work that in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:41:37-07:00","id":888829,"title":"","content":"Might overlap heavily with the Talbot Group (and I'm inclined to just make it the Talbot Group at my table), but I like the idea of a Psychologist group that tries to treat Beasts and Heroes alike to break the cycle of abusive behavior. Of course while healing a Heroes may be possible, there's very little chance of breaking a Beast's need to feed (unless it's a Conspiracy with a special Endowment that can create alternative Satiety through treatment?), but they can at least have the Jungian framework to address what the Primordial Dream represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T00:27:12-07:00","id":888914,"title":"","content":"They could always convince a Beast to get themselves up to Satiety 10 and stay there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888823#post888823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a bad idea. Let me see if I can't work that in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888822#post888822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But those hunters who go above and beyond, those who hunt for pleasure or profit, they're given no quarter<span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Hunting people for profit is <i>exactly</i> what Beasts do all the time. Literally in the case of Collectors, but more metaphorically with a profit of Satiety for everyone else. Sure Beasts can say they need to eat to live. But Cheiron can say they need money to buy food, housing and to invest in medical research. All of which are as vital a component of life as Satiety.<br /> <br /> Hunting for pleasure... I'm not sure if feeding counts as &quot;for pleasure&quot; but there is no shortage of monsters in the WoD who have pleasure as a prime motivation for their hunting. E.G. Sin-Eaters with a particularly sadistic Geist could easily murder people for fun or Slashers who does it for pleasure. Both would be Kin, which means Beasts won't judge them and in encourage them to &quot;To Thy Own Self Be True&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now Beasts can still hate and treat hunters who go for profit and pleasure. I don't think you should change that. But when there's hypocrisy on this scale it means that there's some interesting psychology at play here. I think it should be explored further, we should learn why Beasts feel such rage towards humans who act no worse than family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888822#post888822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> For example, when beasts learn of the Cheiron Group and their morbid Thanatechnology, their typical response is to turn the hunt back on the hunters, to slaughter them, and to slaughter their entire cells. In one egregious example in Tokyo, the Cheiron Group was entirely eradicated by a small group of beasts in order to &quot;reclaim&quot; the bodies of their kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not to keen on this.<br /> <br /> Beasts taking the Cheiron Group's methods personally and hating them for it. Sure, no problem. But a small group of Beasts eradicating an entire devision of a Conspiracy feels wrong. Defeating an entire wing of a Hunter Conspiracy, especially in a Hunter book, isn't something that should be done as an aside example. It's something that should take serious effort on the part of the monsters, and have all the set backs and complications you'd expect from a long conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T00:58:02-07:00","id":888934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888914#post888914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts taking the Cheiron Group's methods personally and hating them for it. Sure, no problem. But a small group of Beasts eradicating an entire devision of a Conspiracy feels wrong. Defeating an entire wing of a Hunter Conspiracy, especially in a Hunter book, isn't something that should be done as an aside example. It's something that should take serious effort on the part of the monsters, and have all the set backs and complications you'd expect from a long conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with that- hunters, while weaker than monsters, should have the advantage of numbers and resources, especially when we are talking about Conspiracies. While eradicating the presence of a certain conspiracy in a certain city by the hands of monsters is possible, it should be clear that it is not a common phenomena- either it was a long/big battle between the two, the monsters used some trickery/exploited some of the group's weakness/caught them by surprise or that Cheiron's presence/interest in Tokyo was not that big in the first place. You know, some justification for their falling- although the word &quot;egregious&quot; does hint that this is the case.<br /> <br /> As for the seeming hypocrisy in how the beasts view hunters- I don't see it. Yeah, Beasts do terrible, terrible things, but they don't do it to their Family, and considering that they were meant to teach mankind through Fear, they can accept that when an hunter come and protect &quot;their Family&quot; against monsters they do it because they learned from their teachings. Hunters who kill for profit and pleasure do so not out of the lessons of the Dark Mother, but from the reasons Beasts hunt after people. In a way, Beasts see hunters through the same lens hunters look at the monsters, and so they uphold a certain &quot;Vigil&quot; of their own to protect their Kin. Just as an hunter may be able to understand that a vampire must drink blood and mages have to chase their obsessions, so does Beasts understand hunters must attack monsters- for this is their nature. But when the vampire slaughter without second thought or the mage kill for Mana, hunters won't be able to &quot;justify&quot; such acts and do all they can to eradicate those monsters- such as Beast act upon hunters like the Abbey or Cheiron. The most interesting parallel is how the Beasts view hunters like the Lucifuge- that is, Kin who turned upon their own. That would make the Devil's Children into the Beasts version of Slashers, wouldn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T01:43:22-07:00","id":888958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888934#post888934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the seeming hypocrisy in how the beasts view hunters- I don't see it. Yeah, Beasts do terrible, terrible things, but they don't do it to their Family</div> </div> </div> </div> Neither do hunters.<br /> <br /> Maybe Cheiron count as family after a few implants, but that wasn't the impression I got. However as an unEndowed Compact Ashwood Abbey surely aren't Kin at all; so they're not doing it to their Family.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888934#post888934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and considering that they were meant to teach mankind through Fear, they can accept that when an hunter come and protect &quot;their Family&quot; against monsters they do it because they learned from their teachings.</div> </div> </div> </div> Beasts who intentionally create Hunters or inspire Hunters to be better at killing monsters would be a very interesting concept.<br /> <br /> E.G. A Beast who inflicts Nightmares themed around the local Apex so that when the targets overcome the Nightmares, they're no longer scared and ready to fight the Apex in the real world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888934#post888934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hunters who kill for profit and pleasure do so not out of the lessons of the Dark Mother, but from the reasons Beasts hunt after people.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. This was more or less my point: &quot;Do as I say, not as I do&quot; is often the motto of the hypocrite.<br /> <br /> Beasts saying &quot;we're aloud to hunt for pleasure and profit, we're monsters. You're supposed to look at us as examples of what not to do, so if you end up like us we will be very <i>very</i> disappointed&quot;. Is an interesting psychological angle, and it should be explored in depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T01:58:05-07:00","id":888961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888958#post888958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Neither do hunters.<br /> <br /> Maybe Cheiron count as family after a few implants, but that wasn't the impression I got. However as an unEndowed Compact Ashwood Abbey surely aren't Kin at all; so they're not doing it to their Family.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that Beasts hate those hunters not because they are &quot;betrayers&quot; like the Lucifuge (that is, that they turn upon their own &quot;Family&quot;), but that they do bad things to the Beast's Family without what a Beast could call a &quot;good reason&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T02:08:32-07:00","id":888968,"title":"","content":"Ah. I get you.<br /> <br /> But since the &quot;reason&quot; Ashwood Abbey Hunt is basically the same as plenty of a Beast's Kin, there's hypocracy, and where there's something interesting that deserves to be explored further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T03:04:21-07:00","id":888986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888968#post888968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. I get you.<br /> <br /> But since the &quot;reason&quot; Ashwood Abbey Hunt is basically the same as plenty of a Beast's Kin, there's hypocracy, and where there's something interesting that deserves to be explored further.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) It'll get explored further. <br /> <br /> 2) Beasts get why hunters do what they do. But they draw a hard line at, say, stealing their body parts and grafting them onto themselves. It's like how most humans a) acknowledge that killing is okay, b) understand that sometimes soldiers have to kill, but c) would flip the fuck out if those soldiers started harvesting and selling enemy organs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T03:24:33-07:00","id":888993,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear it's expanded further. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmmmm.... Any chance of a comparison between Cheiron and a Collector who collects body parts? I know there's that roadkill guy, though to be fair he didn't implant his collection into anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T03:26:01-07:00","id":888994,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure hypocrisy is necessarily an issue.<br /> <br /> Just because a Beast is okay with doing something to a group of people (humanity), doesn't mean they're okay with having that done to them or their Family. This is the same reason that most murderers are probably not okay with getting murdered. There's nothing wrong with allowing that 'hypocrisy' to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:26:05-07:00","id":889097,"title":"","content":"I think if you were to ask a Cheiron cell why they hunt they'd say they hunt for knowledge, with profit just being the means to continue that exploration. You can choose to believe that defense or not, but it doesn't change the fact that <i>they</i> believe it. Is that dichotomy really so different from a Beast? Honestly I'd think Cheiron would be closer to kin than a lot of other hunters. Thaumatechnology blurs the line between mortal and supernatural in an immediate physical way. This is one of the reasons I love them as a Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> Are the Beasts categorically objecting to the fact that Cheiron harvests organs or just that they're harvesting <i>their</i> organs? The latter is always fair, but the first begs further questions. Is it because they're feeling protective of their kin? Would they feel the same way about a Collector or a Promethean doing the same thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:26:26-07:00","id":889098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888994#post888994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure hypocrisy is necessarily an issue.<br /> <br /> Just because a Beast is okay with doing something to a group of people (humanity), doesn't mean they're okay with having that done to them or their Family. This is the same reason that most murderers are probably not okay with getting murdered. There's nothing wrong with allowing that 'hypocrisy' to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet they are still hypocrites. Or racist/speciest. If not both. The point is, they are holding double standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:36:30-07:00","id":889106,"title":"","content":"Honestly the presence of hypocrisy or double standards is fine. It just needs to be acknowledged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:27:06-07:00","id":889357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=888958#post888958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Beasts who intentionally create Hunters or inspire Hunters to be better at killing monsters would be a very interesting concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You good? Not wrapped up too tight? I mean, you're going to be there for a few minutes, so I want you to be nice and comfy. What was that? Could you speak up a little, it's hard to hear you when you mumble like that.*<br /> <br /> <i>Yeesh</i>, I know you're upset, but you really need to watch your language. I mean, do you kiss your mother with that mouth?<br /> Anyway, good job tracking me down. And you did really well getting in here, too. Now, <i>Dick Dastardly's Guide to Hackneyed Villainy</i> requires me to monologue about my motives, so better open your ears!*<br /> <br /> See, here's a thing you may have realized: the world outside your window is a <b>lot</b> darker than most people think it is. I should know; after all, me and my friends are part of that darkness. Most people, they just want to ignore things,go on with their lives, and hope it eats other people instead of them.*<br /> <br /> But not you. You're better than that. When faced with the darkness, you wouldn't, <i>couldn't</i> ignore what was going on. That's good, the world needs more people like you, far more than it need people like me. But you don't care about that right now, do you? You just want to cut down the mean ol' monster that mowed down your big bro (though if you knew what he did to get on my radar, you might not be so keen on avenging him).<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's the way things are going to work. I'm gonna cut you down in a second. Then, you'll have to make a choice. Will you run away and try to live a normal life, knowing how many people are suffering and dying because you chose the easy way out? Will you go and decide there are bigger fish to fry, waiting until later to go after me?*Or will you decide the most important thing in the world is cutting me down, right here, right now? I mean, I'd prefer not to die, thank you very much, but honestly I'd be a lot happier to go down swinging against a hero honestly trying to make the world a better place rather than ending up as a trophy to some over-glorified Hero.<br /> <br /> Okay, I admit, that last part probably didn't make sense to you, but it'd take more exposition than I think you're willing to sit through. I'm about to cut you out, so you only have a few more seconds to decide, little candle. <i><b>What will you do?</b></i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T01:22:23-07:00","id":889736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=889098#post889098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet they are still hypocrites. Or racist/speciest. If not both. The point is, they are holding double standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying they aren't. I'm saying it's not a problem.<br /> <br /> It's far more authentic than removing the double standard in service to the belief that all fictional societies/people must adhere to strictly logical thought patterns. Real people don't even do that.<br /> <br /> (Not saying that anyone has advocated that, mind)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:29:04-07:00","id":890318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=889106#post889106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly the presence of hypocrisy or double standards is fine. It just needs to be acknowledged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. I feel like hypocrisy doesn't get acknowledged much in the real world. It can be. But when you're talking about two groups who only ever rarely interact, and likely don't understand one another's motivations, I think it's a little &quot;tell don't show&quot; to call it out instead of letting the reader take from it what they will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T23:02:45-07:00","id":890445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=890318#post890318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know. I feel like hypocrisy doesn't get acknowledged much in the real world. It can be. But when you're talking about two groups who only ever rarely interact, and likely don't understand one another's motivations, I think it's a little &quot;tell don't show&quot; to call it out instead of letting the reader take from it what they will.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and I don't. If it is presented entirely from the point of view of a narrator character than yes it makes more sense to not acknowledge the hypocrisy. If it is being presented through out of character explanatory text though then I feel that it is necessary to acknowledge it if it exists. Players are more likely to take information in the latter at face value because it is essentially being dictated by authorial voice. They are unlikely to go looking for implication or nuance unless they've been given a reason to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T02:46:21-07:00","id":891056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=887791#post887791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conspiracy: The Dream Warriors<br /> This group takes its inspiration from Nightmare on Elm Street 3. The fact that we\u2019ve never been able to say this in a Chronicles of Darkness book is a crime that I want to correct. Basically, they\u2019re troubled teens trained to be lucid dreamers. In the dreamscapes, they have super powers that look a little like Changeling Oneiromancy (I will make some subtle references that they\u2019re related). Basically, they\u2019re armed in their choice environment, and take the fight to the Beasts in their own realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot begin to say how excited I am to see this group. I am greatly looking forward to seeing what you do with them. There are a couple questions that I hope will be addressed in their description. Does their training prevent them from becoming Heroes or Beasts? Could one of these Dream Warriors end up being Devoured in the course of a battle against a Beast and end up with a shiny new Horror of their very own? What happens to these teens as they grow up? Do they continue to be Dream Warriors, or are their powers something that fades with age? Do they fight against any creatures that interfere with dreams, or is it only Beasts? By which I mean, are these guys purely Beast specialists, or do they tangle with changelings, too? This is one conspiracy that seems like it could have easily been a changeling focused one, so I hope that there will at least be a little bit of attention paid to them as well. I do readily acknowledge that this is the Beasts' chapter, and that the focus will be on Beasts, but a guy can hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:32:30-07:00","id":891068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=891056#post891056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cannot begin to say how excited I am to see this group. I am greatly looking forward to seeing what you do with them. There are a couple questions that I hope will be addressed in their description. Does their training prevent them from becoming Heroes or Beasts? Could one of these Dream Warriors end up being Devoured in the course of a battle against a Beast and end up with a shiny new Horror of their very own? What happens to these teens as they grow up? Do they continue to be Dream Warriors, or are their powers something that fades with age? Do they fight against any creatures that interfere with dreams, or is it only Beasts? By which I mean, are these guys purely Beast specialists, or do they tangle with changelings, too? This is one conspiracy that seems like it could have easily been a changeling focused one, so I hope that there will at least be a little bit of attention paid to them as well. I do readily acknowledge that this is the Beasts' chapter, and that the focus will be on Beasts, but a guy can hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's mention that they sometimes tangle with changelings. And in fact, one of their factions basically ignores the beast focus, and uses their skills to hunt whatever they can. After all, they can walk in dreams. So they can learn all sorts of stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:46:03-07:00","id":891148,"title":"","content":"I do freaking love the idea of a Dream Warriors conspiracy, influenced not at all by the fact that <i>Nightmare on Elm Street 3</i> is one of my favorite movies (and the best one of the series).<br /> <br /> I can't imagine how you could write them without having the Dokken song on repeat, because I totally would.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm doing that already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JDveKxl7Ohs\" data-code=\"JDveKxl7Ohs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JDveKxl7Ohs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T09:02:58-07:00","id":891178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=891068#post891068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's mention that they sometimes tangle with changelings. And in fact, one of their factions basically ignores the beast focus, and uses their skills to hunt whatever they can. After all, they can walk in dreams. So they can learn all sorts of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you very much for letting me know that. I am now more excited than ever to see these guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:42:30-07:00","id":891442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=891148#post891148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do freaking love the idea of a Dream Warriors conspiracy, influenced not at all by the fact that <i>Nightmare on Elm Street 3</i> is one of my favorite movies (and the best one of the series).<br /> <br /> I can't imagine how you could write them without having the Dokken song on repeat, because I totally would.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm doing that already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JDveKxl7Ohs\" data-code=\"JDveKxl7Ohs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/JDveKxl7Ohs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to say that I had that playing while writing. But I did. <br /> <br /> I've resisted the urge to use Patricia Arquette in my art notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T12:23:47-07:00","id":893513,"title":"","content":"Something I thought of while looking at the new spoilers: Are any of the new groups going to be considered Kin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:55:17-07:00","id":893635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/559989-new-mortal-remains-chapter?p=893513#post893513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I thought of while looking at the new spoilers: Are any of the new groups going to be considered Kin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well none of the Compacts would. MAYBE the Dream Warriors... though I doubt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T18:12:15-07:00","id":896431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the